{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:hartree_dimensional_consistency","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"hartree_dimensional_consistency","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L124-L129","doc":"**STRUCTURAL (sorry-free).** The Hartree identity is consistent\nwith dimensional analysis: E_h has units [mass · velocity² · (dimensionless)²]\n= [energy]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:force_carrier_from_hartree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"force_carrier_from_hartree","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L112-L122","doc":"**CONDITIONAL.** If the Hartree derivation holds, then the\nforce-carrier intertwining correspondence\n(prop:force-carrier-intertwining-correspondence) follows —\nthe Hartree energy scale connects electromagnetic and\nstrong-force scales through the categorical α_EM. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:bohr_radius_from_hartree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"bohr_radius_from_hartree","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L100-L110","doc":"**CONDITIONAL.** If the Hartree derivation holds, then\nthe Bohr radius a₀ = ℏ/(m_e·c·α) is categorically derived\n(it's just E_h rearranged). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.canonical","kind":"instance","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L87-L94","doc":"**Faithful instance.** Trivial model discharging the structural dependence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.hartree_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.hartree_identity","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L85-L85","doc":"**Conjectural identity** — the categorical Hartree token\nequals `c₂ · m_e · c_q² · α_EM²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.E_h_cat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.E_h_cat","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The categorical Hartree token computed from the four above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.c_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.c_2","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The conjectural coefficient living in\n`R = ℤ[q^{±1/2}, (q − q⁻¹)⁻¹]` (here represented in the\nsmaller `R_q` for axiomatic purposes — concrete instances\nmay refine to the localisation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.alpha_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.alpha_sq","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L75-L75","doc":"The categorical-side fine-structure constant squared. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.c_q_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.c_q_sq","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The categorical-side speed-of-light squared. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.m_e_cat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.m_e_cat","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The categorical-side electron-mass token. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EHartreeCategoricalDerivation","kind":"class","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L46-L85","doc":"**Conjecture class.** An instance asserts the categorical\nHartree-energy identity\n\n  `E_h = c₂ · m_e · c_q² · α_EM²`\n\nin `R_q`, with the coefficient `c₂` arising from `J^1`-vanishing\nin the molecular LP dual.\n\nA concrete instance must supply:\n\n1.  the `q`-dimension decoration `δ_q : NF basis → R_q` whose\n    existence is the categorical input — represented here as\n    the abstract field `q_dim_decoration`;\n2.  the coefficient `c₂ : R_q`;\n3.  the conjectural identity `hartree_identity` linking\n    `c₂`, `m_e^cat`, `c_q^cat`, and `α_EM^cat` in the categorical\n    ground ring.\n\nDownstream blocks may take `[EHartreeCategoricalDerivation]`\nas an explicit hypothesis to remain `theorem` / `proposition`\nper AGENTS.md §3b-cond.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] §Hartree-energy categorical derivation ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:e-hartree-categorical-derivation","label":"conj:e-hartree-categorical-derivation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.R_q","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/e-hartree-categorical-derivation.lean#L42-L44","doc":"The Laurent ground ring `R = ℤ[q^{±1}]` (the localisation at\n`(q − q⁻¹)` is taken externally where needed). ","signatureChunk":0}]}